
# ---- GOLDEN FIXTURE (bridge tile) ----
# resetMode=loadvm -> QMP human-monitor-command "loadvm golden" (live, no reboot).
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
# The CPC's keyboard matrix is scanned by the PSG once per 50 Hz frame (20 ms).
# Browser typing leaves ~2 ms between one key's release and the next key's press,
# so the machine never samples the all-keys-up state and reads a typed line as
# one long chord -- most of the characters are lost. Hold and gap were 2 frames
# (40/40), the margin measured on mpf2.
# 80/80 since 2026-10-04: Caprice32 runs inside a kiosk GUEST, and when labhost
# is loaded that guest stalls, so one key's press and release (or a repeated
# key's release and re-press) reach Caprice32 in the same frame however far
# apart the daemon sent them. Measured through a sandbox daemon, a 12-line
# stress listing read back from LIST: 40/40 lost 1 to 11 keys in 12 of 12
# passes at 1-min load 25-60 (`$$` -> `$`, `110` -> `10`); 80/80 was exact in
# 5 of 6 at load 35-54. Nothing survives load 70+. typeIn/demoProgram
# perCharMs 170 covers HOLD+GAP = 160.
# No SH_KEY_MOD_LEAD_MS: no shifted key arrived unshifted in about 3,800 at
# lead 0, and a lead did not change the losses above (docs/TYPE-IN-EDITOR.md).
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=80
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=80
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Amstrad CPC 6128 Locomotive BASIC yellow-on-blue Ready prompt in Caprice32 (cap32); explicit key down/up keyboard path certified with PRINT, RETURN, and RUN; keyboard-only exhibit; AY-3-8912->ALSA->AC97. Keyboard pacing: SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=80 and SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=80 hold each key and space successive keys by 4 CPC frames (the CPC's matrix is scanned by the PSG once per 50 Hz frame = 20 ms); without the gap, back-to-back typing never lets the machine sample the all-keys-up state and it reads one long chord, and the extra margin over 2 frames rides out the kiosk guest's own stalls under host load.
